  "compatibility": {
    "assumptions": [
      "Docker Desktop Linux backend on Windows and approved Docker Engine on Linux are the only v1 host classes.",
      "The trusted exact-base policy pins the accepted engine/API, immutable base/workload/relay image digests, runtime package-lock, entrypoint/context digests, network policy, resources, mounts, fixed registry subjects, and real probe suite.",
      "S0-S7 are preparatory, and candidate implementation plus Phase-A PR tests for S0-S8 use the legacy unsandboxed bootstrap; they are not managed activation or confinement proof.",
      "The trusted post-merge main workflow, not a candidate or workload container, builds, signs images, creates explicit keyless cosign SLSA attestations, separately verifies signatures and attestations, and publishes the immutable image-lock output consumed by S8.",
      "Per-run named Docker volumes and an independent full Git clone replace writable binds of linked worktrees and repository-global Git storage.",
      "Managed v1 does not load @zosmaai/pi-llm-wiki; mutation and read-only wiki retrieval are absent unless a separately authenticated future capability is approved.",
      "Managed resume and retained recovery are disabled fail-closed in v1; a future authenticated rebind is a separate change.",
      "Missing, queued, skipped, or failing trusted Windows runner/evidence leaves post-merge activation pending/unsupported or blocked and cannot permit the canary or activation; it does not change the Phase-A S8 merge gate under existing protected checks.",
      "The post-S8 ruleset transition changes only future-PR required contexts, is performed by the separately authenticated administrator/trusted controller after Phase-B evidence, and requires A211-T08 revalidation; marker-v3, receipt-v1, DCO, review, lease, and human-only merge authority remain unchanged.",
      "Existing packet-v3, receipt-v1, marker-v3, DCO, protected CI, independent review, lease, and human-only merge gates remain authoritative."
    ],
    "preserves_v1_readability": true,
    "silently_upgrades_v1": false
  },
